unction → antisense/inverted copy)\n18. (128693808,128693894,-1): 5 — SET region\n19. (110244218,110244775,+1): 5\n20. (99222642,99227896,-1): 5\n21. (111664588,111666812,-1): 5 — inverted GNG10 copy\n22. (19376649,19378364,+1): 4 — hmm, this corresponds to RPS6 intron (19376652,19378367) shifted by -3.\n\nPattern: most novel junctions are shifted versions of annotated introns (same coordinates ±1-3 bp, either strand), i.e., from inverted duplication copies of highly expressed genes, or from annotation-version shifts.\n\nThe exception is the GNG10 pair: (111661713,111664533) and (111664590,111666814) — these don't match any annotated intron even with a shift (annotated intron 1 = 111661716-111666814, a single intron; there's no annotated intron ending at 111664533 or starting at 111664590). These define interval 111664534-111664589 (56 bp) inside GNG10 intron 1. This is the cryptic exon!\n\nWait, but let me also verify (125238827,125238939) etc. in the HSPA5 region: HSPA5 annotated introns: (125237155,125238140), (125238309,125238589), (125238828,125238940), (125239332,125239420), (125239534,125240171), (125240310,125240675), (125240908,125241004). Observed novel: (125237153,125238138,+1,4): shifted by -2; (125238827,125238939,+1,4): shifted by -1; (125239532,125240169,+1,9): shifted by -2; (125240308,125240673,+1,4): shifted by -2; (125240908,125241004, both strands 5-6): perfect match → annotated. So HSPA5 plus-strand junctions are all shifted annotated introns → HSPA5 is on the minus strand, so these plus-strand junctions are the inverted copy. Trap again.\n\nAnd the minus-strand junctions in the HSPA5 region match HSPA5's introns: (125239534,125240171,-1,11) = perfect match with annotated → annotated ✓ (probe16 shows both).\n\nSimilarly, the SET region (128.69 Mb, plus strand): minus-strand junctions are shifted versions of SET's introns (inverted copy); plus-strand ones match SET's introns (annotated).\n\nANP32B (plus strand): (97994779,97998553,-1,5) minus — h