Many additional novel junctions were detected (see `junctions.tsv`), but they
are shifted (+/-1-3 bp) copies of annotated introns, frequently on the
opposite strand, produced by reads from inverted segmental-duplication copies
of highly expressed genes (RPS6, RPL7A, HSPA5, SET, ...). Every interval
defined by those junction pairs overlaps an annotated exon (the shifted exon
of the duplicated copy), so none qualifies as a cryptic exon. The GNG10 pair
is the only pair of well-supported novel junctions whose intervening interval
is unannotated, gene-internal, and expressed.

